{
  "schema": 1,
  "name": "A Wildcard Hero at the level cap rapid rolls with Scrolls of Fortune until a desired entry",
  "contract": "On Darkmoon - Season 10 Wildcard a Hero at the level cap without unspent essence could rapid roll (C_Wildcard.StartRapidRolling, enabled by CONFIG_WILDCARD_QUICK_ROLLING_ENABLED): the client unlearned the newest undesired entry with a Scroll of Fortune (CMSG 0x61D, CA_UNLEARN_OK) and sent CMSG 0x643 {u32 roll count, u32 n x desired entry id, u32 n x desired SpellTagTypes id, u8 is-ability}. The server answered SMSG 0x644 CAN_START_RAPID_ROLLING_OK and rerolled on its own, one Scroll of Fortune per roll after the first, until an entry of the desired list (or with a desired spell tag) came up (STOP_RAPID_ROLLING_DESIRED_ENTRY_LEARNED) or the count or the scrolls ran out (STOP_RAPID_ROLLING_COUNT_DEPLETED); only the kept entry was revealed (SMSG 0x621 {u32 entry, u32 ranks, stop code}). Refusals came as CAN_START_RAPID_ROLLING_* in SMSG 0x644: NOT_MAX_LEVEL, NO_DESIRED_ENTRIES, UNSPENT_ABILITY/TALENT_ESSENCE, NO_ROLL, TOO_HIGH_COUNT. The rerolls of each kind were counted per spec (SMSG 0x6EE at login, 0x6EF on change) against the quick-roll configs (SMSG 0x6F0 {u8 is-ability, u32 threshold, u32 max}) that allow longer sessions: 5 scrolls at first, up to 10 (Discord; this realm unlocks 10 at 50 rerolls, the threshold is not known).",
  "timeout_ms": 120000,
  "players": [
    {"id": "wild", "race": 1, "class": 10, "level": 1}
  ],
